<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">raise-skeleton</ansi> spell

The <ansi fg="command">Raise Skeleton</ansi> spell animates the bones of a nearby corpse,
stripping flesh and sinew away to leave a rattling skeleton servant under
your command. The weakest of the raised undead, but requiring little essence
to conjure. Almost any corpse will do.

Skeletons are fast and fragile, striking with swift melee attacks but
lacking the durability of their heavier undead kin. They move with jarring,
brittle grace.

The undead servant's power scales with your willpower and spellcasting skill.
More skilled casters summon more formidable specimens.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">cast raise-skeleton [corpse]</ansi>     Animate nearby remains.

<ansi fg="yellow">Base Folds:  </ansi> Brief channel
<ansi fg="yellow">Corpse:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Requires weak remains</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Target:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Nearby corpse or ground loot</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Conv. Cost:  </ansi> Modest
<ansi fg="yellow">School:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Manifestation</ansi>

<ansi fg="white-bold">Notes:</ansi>
  - The skeleton appears under your command and aids you in combat.
  - Once raised, the undead servant remains active as a companion.
  - Use the <ansi fg="command">assess</ansi> command to evaluate a corpse's quality.

